{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>המעמך ישלמנה</b> — Most of the commentators went astray on this verse. Some say: המעמך ישלם — the lack of my understanding, for you rejected my words. And some say: המעמך — is there power with you to settle the evil with you, to make peace, for you will choose my words if I speak truth. And what seems correct to me is: it is thus, המעמך ישלם — the evil or the good." "<b>כי מאסת</b> — And the meaning: there are people who will say, I do not want to suffer evil in exchange for a great good whose reward will come, as in the case of לא הם ולא שכרם (neither they nor their reward)." "<b>כי אתה תבחר ולא אני</b> — And why do you choose — or perhaps I would want to suffer a little evil for a brief time, in exchange for much good for days without end."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "Resolved רובי המפרשים as 'most of the commentators'; the syntax of the second opinion is difficult and translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:33.805990915Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}